# Colour This / Color Sound Template

Use the current **test color-sound game** as the reference implementation when building or iterating color-sound games for other vocabulary card sets.

## Canonical Reference

- Template page: `client/src/pages/primary/test/test.color-sound.tsx`
- Shared engine: `client/src/components/games/ColourThisGame.tsx`
- Test data pattern: `client/src/data/test-primary-vocab.ts`
- Prefer SVG image sets with full-region targets over PNG hint-circle behavior.

## Current UX To Preserve

- For SVG/full-region mode, clues use a semi-transparent progressive fill over each target color area.
- Image target arrows are small, thick arrows that point at the target, move forward/backward in unison, and may briefly disappear randomly before returning.
- When the correct picture color is applied, reveal the true color immediately; the arrow becomes a brief tick/check mark and disappears.
- The square image area should stay centered against the pencil sidebar.
- Selected pencil starts larger, pulses larger in place, and sits slightly left compared with the other pencils.

## Word Clue Behavior

- The word should also get a progressive semi-transparent fill clue for uncolored letters.
- The word arrow belongs just to the left of the first letter and points right toward the word.
- The word arrow stays until the whole word is colored correctly, then turns into a tick/check mark at the same spot and disappears.

## Future Rollout Guidance

When adapting other vocab sets, copy the test set’s interaction model first, then adjust only data/assets unless the user explicitly asks for a gameplay change.
